  "title": "A freeze creates no reservation and preserves committed/exposed accounting; existing exposed keeps counting (KS-7)",
  "spec": ["SPEC §5.4", "SPEC §7", "SPEC §3.4", "ADR-026", "ADR-027"],
  "description": "SPEC §5.4 (KS-7): a freeze is a stop-future-authorization control, never a rollback. R1 is committed (3) and R2 is exposed (4) before the scope is frozen. While frozen, a new reserve R3 is denied with TX402_SPEND_FROZEN — no reservation is created — yet the snapshot is byte-for-byte identical to the pre-freeze one except `frozen: true`: committed 3, exposed 4, cumulativeConsumed 7 all keep counting, and the exposed R2 is still held. Unfreezing changes only `frozen` back to false; every committed/exposed figure is preserved. A freeze cannot revoke a transmitted signature.",
